From: pbs05 <27010143+pbs05@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: use the shared port lock for MIB stats

The AN7581 phylink patch uses the port lock for MIB reads and GDM4
fragment register updates. Keep the lossless MIB reader on that lock.

Signed-off-by: lean <chenlin@fnnas.com>

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2075,7 +2075,7 @@ static void airoha_update_hw_stats(struct airoha_gdm_dev *dev)
 	u32 val, i = 0;
 	u64 data;
 
-	spin_lock(&port->stats_lock);
+	spin_lock(&port->lock);
 
 	/* Read relevant MIB for GDM with multiple port attached */
 	if (port->id == AIROHA_GDM3_IDX || port->id == AIROHA_GDM4_IDX)
@@ -2269,6 +2269,6 @@ static void airoha_update_hw_stats(struct airoha_gdm_dev *dev)
 	u64_stats_update_end(&dev->stats.syncp);
 
-	spin_unlock(&port->stats_lock);
+	spin_unlock(&port->lock);
 }
 
 static void airoha_update_netdev_features(struct airoha_gdm_dev *dev)
